WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:05.730
You can just follow your "List" or check out
the "what's new" or "what's hot" tabs, or

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:11.620
you can dig a little deeper into the Netflix
archives to find some truly outstanding, under-the-radar

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:12.120
films.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:16.219
Here's a look at some of the best stuff to
add to your queue the next time you don't

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:16.960
know what to watch.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:22.400
The Duffer Brothers might allude to their
Spielbergian influences and aims in Stranger

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:28.000
Things, but Rim of the World director McG
unabashedly and cheerfully made an '80s-style

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:28.900
kid adventure movie.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.559
Rim of the World mixes elements of E.T., The
Goonies, and Red Dawn to create a similarly

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.400
fun sci-fi action movie where teens save the
day.

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.800
"If you find yourself alone, riding in green
fields with the sun on your face, do not be

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.300
troubled.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.460
For you are in Elysium.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:46.380
And you are already dead."

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:52.039
The simple, irresistible premise: four kids
arrive at summer camp just in time for an

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.220
invasion of the planet by wicked aliens.

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:59.260
With the well-populated "Rim of the World"
camp soon abandoned, it's up to this ragtag

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:03.500
group of teens who don't quite fit in elsewhere
to come together and thwart what amounts to

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.440
the end of the world.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:09.500
They'll have to do it all without adults,
computers, or much of anything… except,

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.900
of course, for bikes.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.560
Heaven of Horror says of this lightweight
diversion:

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.080
"This is an absolute treat for fans of sci-fi,
adventure, action, and monster movies."

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.020
After bringing so much attention and accolades
to Netflix via his unforgettable performance

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.360
as Sheriff Hopper on Stranger Things, it's
no surprise that David Harbour has free reign

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:31.340
to do whatever he wants at the streaming giant.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.979
And what he wants to do is a meta, sci-fi
and horror-laced mockumentary about his life,

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:40.200
a collaboration with Arrested Development
writer John Levenstein.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.840
The result is a short special that's a bit
hard to define.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:50.300
Frankenstein's Monster's Monster, Frankenstein
is based around a mid-1970s made-for-TV production

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:52.920
of the two-man theatrical version of Frankenstein.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:58.880
The twist is that Harbour plays his own "father,"
also an actor named David Harbour, as the

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:03.980
two generations play both Dr. Frankenstein
and his monstrous creation at the same time.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:07.979
To round out this tribute from the younger
Harbour to the fictional older Harbour are

00:02:07.979 --> 00:02:12.790
clips of the actor from other vintage fictional
productions like The Crying Detective and

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:13.720
The Actor's Trunk.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:18.040
The whole thing winds up both a love letter
to the craft of acting and an affectionate

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.780
send-up of the entire notion of playing pretend
for a living.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:28.220
This 2017 indie horror movie by writer/director
Trey Edward Shults feels like an old-fashioned

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:29.140
kind of horror movie.

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.700
Sure, it trades in spooky monsters and frightening
imagery, but it's more about conjuring up

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:38.880
what's already inside the viewer: the unspeakable
dread of things yet to come.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.220
It Comes at Night is set deep in a remote
woodland area not long after an epidemic has

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.020
wiped out most human life on earth.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.120
It's where the small family of Paul, Sarah,
and young Travis try to survive on what little

00:02:51.129 --> 00:02:55.080
supplies they've got and hope they don't get
infected with the plague.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:59.410
But then danger comes looking for them in
the form of a roving family man named Will,

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.360
who is maybe not the innocent guy he claims
to be.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:02.940
"Hey, listen.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.120
I don't even have to shoot you, you know?

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.800
I could just leave you out here.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.440
You want this water?"

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:08.060
"Yeah."

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.500
"Make me believe you."

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:15.020
Still, Sarah invites Will and his family into
their homestead on the theory of strength

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.020
in numbers, but that only seems to invite
more danger...

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.610
most of it impossibly horrific, lurking out
there in the forest.

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:26.150
The London Evening Standard's Charlotte O'Sullivan
said of the film:

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:29.969
"It made me so tense I could hardly breathe,
let alone think."

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:35.340
Vietnam is home to a quickly developing movie
culture and industry, and the action thriller

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.860
Furie teams up two of its stars, director
Le-Van Kiet and actress Veronica Ngo , best

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.440
known to Western audiences as gunner Paige
Tico in Star Wars: The Last Jedi.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:51.360
In Furie, Ngo portrays a former criminal overlord
who now works as the muscle for a loan shark

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.180
in the city of Can Tho, shaking down delinquents
with a shattering of a kneecap or two.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:01.060
That violence comes home to roost when her
daughter, Mai, is kidnapped and seemingly

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.140
sold to black market organ dealers.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:09.099
Ngo, propelled by equal parts rage, guilt,
and love, takes to the seedy sides of Ho Chi

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.180
Minh City to get her daughter back in one
piece.

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:16.790
Furie is a tight, often sparse ride, which
includes plenty of novel set pieces, beautiful

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.660
cinematography, and an intense motorbike chase.

00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:25.180
Sometimes the scariest parts of a scary movie
don't come from monsters or gore, but from

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.420
menace and dread.

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:31.440
That's what propels the precisely paced Earthquake
Bird, based on the novel of the same name

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.560
by Susanna Jones.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.500
Alicia Vikander of Ex Machina returns to the
kind of moody, unsettling cinema that made

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.200
her famous, portraying Lucy, a Swedish expatriate
who has settled into a life in 1989 Tokyo

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.400
that is repetitive, bland, and mundane.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:51.520
It's by design, as she's looking to flee from
and forget past traumas.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:55.540
She works as a translator, living alone while
maintaining some low-key friendships and playing

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:56.820
cello in a string quartet.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:02.040
One day, Lucy meets Teiji, a noodle shop worker
and aspiring photographer.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.820
She enchants him and lets him make portraits
of her.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:07.080
"I've never had my picture taken before.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:09.080
Not properly."

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:12.320
"Then, I'm the first."

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.840
But just when it seems like her icy veneer
is starting to thaw, Lucy's life is interrupted

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:21.260
by a brash American named Lily, who goes missing
and is presumed dead.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:27.110
Is the mysterious Lucy responsible, either
via conscious act or her status as a tragedy

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:27.600
magnet?

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.220
Or is she merely an unreliable narrator?

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.420
Gabriel Silver of the Detroit Metro Times
said:

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.810
"Earthquake Bird is an enjoyable neo-noir
film, with enough twists and turns to leave

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.560
you thinking long after the ending."

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:45.180
Yes, it's a thriller set at a lake deep in
the woods, and a young person dies very early

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.100
on in the movie.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:50.520
Apart from that setup and the notion that
an unrepentant killer could strike at any

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:55.040
time Every Time I Die is as far away as can
be from your typical horror.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:06:00.080
The film follows the forlorn Sam, who is still
recovering from the childhood tragedy of losing

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:01.180
a sister to drowning.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.810
Now a paramedic, he keeps his mind off of
his troubles with an ongoing affair with a

00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:11.410
married woman that is, until he's killed at
the hands of her husband, returning soldier

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:11.900
Tyler.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:14.860
That's when Every Time I Die takes a turn.

00:06:15.260 --> 00:06:19.620
Drew's unsettled consciousness floats into
the bodies of his friends, attempting to warn

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.740
them that they could be the next to die.

00:06:22.150 --> 00:06:26.960
The film's tightly-packed 98 minute running
time and minuscule budget serve it well, as

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.040
it winds up a rarity in cinema: a pensive
thriller.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:34.010
Andrew Stover of Film Inquiry said of Every
Time I Die:

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:38.680
"It's a captivating little tale about self-image,
with a mystical and poignant touch."

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.800
Don is just a regular guy, a lawyer whose
life has taken a few bad turns because of

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.980
his own bad decisions.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:49.820
Seeking a fresh start before his wife Liz
gives birth to their first child, he buys

00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.780
a decrepit old house way out in suburban Chicago.

00:06:53.210 --> 00:06:57.780
He moves in first, so that he can pour himself
into renovating this old, spooky manor.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:02.240
Somehow, Don doesn't go screaming back into
the city when he discovers that the house

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:07.620
bleeds and excretes a strange white fluid
out of its pipes, or when he keeps discovering

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.800
human and animal corpses and freaky, ghostly
monsters.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:15.840
As if all that isn't enough, he's got to contend
with a flirty neighbor who may know more about

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:18.370
the source of the house's horrors than she's
letting on.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:23.200
Girl on the Third Floor marks the screenwriting
and directorial debut of veteran horror producer

00:07:23.200 --> 00:07:24.240
Travis Stevens.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.160
The haunted house movie is a well-traveled
genre, but Stevens tweaks the formula enough

00:07:29.160 --> 00:07:31.960
to leave audiences guessing, entertained,
and unsettled.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:37.120
Based on the originality and success of The
Matrix, Hollywood has frequently given the

00:07:37.130 --> 00:07:42.520
Wachowskis a blank check to make whatever
visually dazzling, unabashedly earnest, and

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.340
totally bonkers sci-fi movie they felt like
making.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:51.200
One of those movies is Jupiter Ascending,
which stars Mila Kunis as Jupiter Jones, a

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.900
Russian-American house cleaner and amateur
astronomer.

00:07:54.350 --> 00:07:58.600
Through a string of events that involves selling
her eggs to pay for a telescope, she finds

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.880
out she's some kind of space princess.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:07.440
The Abrasax clan, a prominent galactic family,
wants her dead, or maybe just control of her

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:07.940
birthright.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:13.690
Fortunately, she's got the steadfast protection
from Caine Wise, played by Channing Tatum,

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:16.500
a half-human/half-wolf super-soldier.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:22.040
Jupiter Ascending is a bit of an overstuffed
sci-fi extravaganza, and it has everything,

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:27.560
from jet packs to giant spaceships to hand-to-hand
combat to Sean Bean playing a rogue bee-man.

00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:33.580
Stephanie Cooke of Rogues Portal manages to
sum up the film's many joys in one pithy remark:

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:38.340
"Ever wondered what Cinderella, The Godfather,
and Teen Wolf would be like if they were one

00:08:38.340 --> 00:08:38.840
movie?"

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:39.780
"No?

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:42.300
Well, too bad because Jupiter Ascending exists."

00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:47.220
"Not a pretty sight… snipped and stripped,
the mark of a court martial skyjacking.”

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.380
You still haven’t answered my question do
you want your wings back or not?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:51.880
“Wait, you had wings?"

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:57.120
Why are period horror films so much scarier
than ones set in the modern day?

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:02.300
Is it because the relative ignorance and brutality
of the past adds an extra element of terror?

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:08.120
Or are images of Victorian-era Londoners in
bleak clothes living bleak lives inherently

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:08.760
unsettling?

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:14.060
That could be the answer, although blood-hungry
monsters, freaky islands, and blood cults

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:15.900
are scary too.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.920
Fortunately, Apostle showcases all that and
much more.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:26.240
Set in 1905, Apostle follows a man named Thomas,
who leaves London for an island paradise off

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.420
the coast of Wales.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:32.860
It's run by a cult, and Thomas must retrieve
his sister, taken to the island by the group

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:34.060
and held for ransom.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:39.139
He poses as a new adherent to gain favor with
the cult members and their leader, Prophet

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.840
Malcolm, all while aiming to get his sister
back.

00:09:42.029 --> 00:09:46.700
However, things get awfully sticky for Thomas
when he realizes that the cult's teachings

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:48.460
aren't exactly crazy.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:53.260
Those jars of blood everyone carries around
to collect their blood sacrifice to the island?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.220
The island needs that blood.

00:09:55.540 --> 00:10:00.020
Imagine if Little Shop of Horrors mashed up
with The Wicker Man and you've got Apostle.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:03.260
"She gifted me her wisdom.

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:10.260
She trusted me that I may enrich your minds."

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:16.600
According to the thoughtful sci-fi movie Io,
humanity is doomed to never change its ways,

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:20.470
and in the not-too-distant future, Earth becomes
uninhabitable.

00:10:20.470 --> 00:10:26.230
Fortunately, scientists have found a new home
for mankind on Io, one of Jupiter's many moons.

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:30.670
A scientist named Sam is among the handful
of humans who haven't made the migration to

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:35.160
Io just yet, staying behind to test the water
and air for signs of decreasing toxicity,

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:40.370
as well as to raise bees that she hopes could
someday pollinate and help save the planet's

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:40.880
vegetation.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:46.579
Time is running out, and certain catastrophic
events lead Sam to head with another survivor,

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:49.249
Micah, to a shuttle that will take them into
space.

00:10:49.249 --> 00:10:54.279
Io is full of philosophical and mental tension
as these two bear witness to what could be

00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:58.720
Earth's final, extinctive whimper, but also
a newfound hope for the future.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:02.180
Leigh Monson of Birth.Movies.Death. says:

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:07.820
"If you're looking for science fiction that
makes manifest the anxieties of a dying world,

00:11:07.829 --> 00:11:11.060
our dying world, then Io is a good place to
start."

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:12.500
"We weren't ready for this.

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:18.180
No matter what warning we got from your father."

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:21.140
What if John Wick were more like an '80s movie?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:27.790
More violent, more nihilistic, more violence-soaked
and with more absolutely unnecessary nudity,

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:31.280
all with a gleeful undercurrent of shock humor
permeating the whole thing?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:37.700
That's Polar, the bonkers, messy story of
one man's quest to relax and secure his pension.

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:42.760
Mads Mikkelsen, the Danish actor best known
for his starring role on the stylish TV version

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:47.459
of Hannibal, stars as Duncan Vizla, a.k.a.
the Black Kaiser.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:52.720
Duncan is a highly effective assassin forced
by his oddly corporate bosses to retire at

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.300
age 50 and enjoy his golden years.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.880
Of course, his company plans to kill him off
to avoid paying his payout.

00:11:59.320 --> 00:12:03.639
From a lovely cabin in Montana, Duncan has
to fight off some violent attacks while also

00:12:03.640 --> 00:12:08.220
dealing with PTSD and forging a friendship
with a neighbor with demons of her own.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.280
"I know they pay you well for this Vivian.

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.200
I’m still going to give you a chance to
walk out of here alive.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:16.420
For old time's sake."

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:19.140
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:19.140 --> 00:12:22.520
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:12:22.770 --> 00:12:25.920
